From: CoreELEC Xiaomi SMB3 Multichannel laboratory
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL R3] cifs: use least-loaded channel for non-binding requests

Backport the core selector behavior from Linux upstream:
  ea90708d3cf3d0d92c02afe445ad463fb3c6bf10 cifs: use the least loaded channel for sending requests

The CoreELEC vendor 5.15.196 tree has a binding-specific branch in
cifs_pick_channel() that is not present in the original upstream context.
Preserve that vendor behavior and change only the non-binding multichannel
selector.

For multiple channels:
- inspect server->in_flight;
- select the least-loaded channel;
- disregard advertised link speed;
- fall back to the existing round-robin selector when all channels are
  equally loaded.

Deliberately NOT included here:
  66d590b828b1fd9fa337047ae58fe1c4c6f43609 cifs: deal with the channel loading lag while picking channels

That follow-up remains isolated for R3.1 so R3 can be measured causally.

--- a/fs/cifs/transport.c
+++ b/fs/cifs/transport.c
@@ -1039,16 +1039,42 @@
 struct TCP_Server_Info *cifs_pick_channel(struct cifs_ses *ses)
 {
 	uint index = 0;
+	unsigned int min_in_flight = UINT_MAX, max_in_flight = 0;
+	struct TCP_Server_Info *server = NULL;
+	int i;
 
 	if (!ses)
 		return NULL;
 
 	spin_lock(&ses->chan_lock);
 	if (!ses->binding) {
-		/* round robin */
 		if (ses->chan_count > 1) {
-			index = (uint)atomic_inc_return(&ses->chan_seq);
-			index %= ses->chan_count;
+			for (i = 0; i < ses->chan_count; i++) {
+				server = ses->chans[i].server;
+				if (!server)
+					continue;
+
+				/*
+				 * strictly speaking, we should pick up req_lock to read
+				 * server->in_flight. But it shouldn't matter much here if we
+				 * race while reading this data. The worst that can happen is
+				 * that we could use a channel that's not least loaded. Avoiding
+				 * taking the lock could help reduce wait time, which is
+				 * important for this function
+				 */
+				if (server->in_flight < min_in_flight) {
+					min_in_flight = server->in_flight;
+					index = i;
+				}
+				if (server->in_flight > max_in_flight)
+					max_in_flight = server->in_flight;
+			}
+
+			/* if all channels are equally loaded, fall back to round-robin */
+			if (min_in_flight == max_in_flight) {
+				index = (uint)atomic_inc_return(&ses->chan_seq);
+				index %= ses->chan_count;
+			}
 		}
 		spin_unlock(&ses->chan_lock);
 		return ses->chans[index].server;
